WHY THIS FILE EXISTS

A copyleft licence is enforced by the copyright holder. Until this file existed, Keel
named no holder anywhere in the tree — the workspace manifest said only "Keel
contributors" — which would have made the AGPL on this code very hard to act on. This
file is the record. It is not a formality.

Authorship of record is the commit history. Keel takes contributions under the Developer
Certificate of Origin with no copyright assignment, so each contributor holds copyright in
what they wrote, and the copyright in the whole is held jointly. Nobody, the maintainers
included, can relicense another contributor's work as proprietary software.


LICENSING

Except for the two crates listed below, Keel is licensed under the GNU Affero General
Public License, version 3 or (at your option) any later version, together with the
additional permission in LICENSE-EXCEPTION.md.

    Full licence text ..... LICENSE
    Additional permission . LICENSE-EXCEPTION.md
    SPDX identifier ....... AGPL-3.0-or-later

Two crates are deliberate exceptions, because a copyleft licence would stop the thing they
exist to do — be spoken to, and be embedded — while protecting nothing. Neither of them
can reach key material, the cryptographic core, or the vault format; the layering rule in
xtask/src/rules.rs enforces that, and `cargo xtask check-licenses` enforces that their
dependency closures stay permissive.

    crates/keel-proto ..... Apache-2.0   (LICENSE-APACHE-2.0)
    crates/keel-client .... MPL-2.0      (LICENSE-MPL-2.0)

Every source file states its own licence in an SPDX header, so no file's terms depend on
finding this one. See docs/architecture.md for why the licence boundary sits exactly where
the dependency boundary already sat.


WHAT THE LICENCE DOES AND DOES NOT COVER

The AGPL covers the code. It does not cover the name. "Keel" and the Keel logo are
trademarks of the copyright holder; forks are welcome and must rebrand. See TRADEMARK.md.

Third-party dependency licences are enumerated and enforced in deny.toml, and checked in
CI by cargo-deny.
